    "demoUrl": "https://vincentwei1021.github.io/mg-styles-15/#{id}"
  },
  "motionPrompt": {
    "_about": "Motion Prompt (Shohei Ohtaki, MIT): 168 names in 7 packs for the things you ask an AI to make (motion graphics, camera moves, UI, landing page, photo looks), each with a one-line meaning, an example ask, its numbers in words and the author's Canvas 2D sample (SOURCES M08). The Library's fourth type \"Vocabulary\" under author Shohei Ohtaki: words and numbers for Claude, not runnable motions. The read-only clone at the pinned commit; the app reads api/v1 (catalog.json, en/e/<id>.txt, kit/<pack>.js), LICENSE and THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md from it, as shipped, and never edits it. Not used: the author's skill and CLI, the gallery, make-your-own, examples/found.json (other people's posts). Update: git fetch in the clone, git diff --stat <pin>..origin/main -- packs api, run tools/intake-motion-prompt.mjs (replaces items by number), re-pin after the maintainer's OK",
    "repo": "showheyohtaki/motion-prompt",
    "commit": "bd6bf08d8d412cc82c1bbc8f1a81638617a45cfb",
    "date": "2026-10-23",
    "licence": "MIT (Copyright (c) 2026 Shohei Ohtaki)",
    "root": "{app}/bundle/styles/motion-prompt",
    "demoUrl": "https://showheyohtaki.github.io/motion-prompt/#{id}"
  },
  "anidoodle": {
    "_about": "anidoodle (Alex Greenshpun, 10x Company): a skill and a TypeScript engine that draw pictures and films entirely in code in 32 media (SOURCES M10). The read-only clone at the pinned commit; the app reads skills/anidoodle (SKILL.md, references/, the engine's src/) from it, never edits it, and bundles a film's own module with the engine through esbuild. Apache-2.0 with NOTICE.",
